ependent polling confirms or contradicts the GBAO result in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Brad Finstad (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Brad Finstad seeks a second full term in a southern Minnesota district that leans Republican by about six points, in what appears to be a favorable national environment for his party. He has raised roughly $2 million and holds a modest cash advantage over DFL nominee Jake Johnson, who has matched him on the money front and campaigned aggressively across all 21 counties.\n\nRatings are split: several outlets call the race Likely R, while others, including Cook after an August downgrade, rate it Lean R. A late September GBAO poll showed Johnson up a point, though it came from a Democratic-leaning sponsor, and prediction markets still give Finstad roughly a three-in-four chance. The race is competitive but tilts Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1904, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.19, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1925, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3207, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2388, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2075, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.271, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3469, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2769, "margin": -4.0}]}